# The RP renders a closed job as an FX-80 prints it and writes it as a PDF:
# our ESC/P pages (TEXT.PRN then GRAPH.PRN, sent by PRFILES as in hook-escp)
# become one job, read back from the card once it closes and rendered a
# little at a time in the main loop. Its three pages must be the pixels the
# host test draws for the two files (tools/printer/golden/TEXT.PRN.pages and
# GRAPH.PRN.pages): the debug build logs each page's MD5. The PDF must be the
# one tools/printer/render writes for the same bytes (make_bench_disks.sh's
# escp-expected.pdf), and the job deleted once it is.
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/escp.st
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
log "pages: job 00000001 page 1 1985x2526 MD5 3b96f3a221f886f6629eeccbade871f8" 3000
log "pages: job 00000001 page 2 1985x2526 MD5 d8e2c2cb7b4b1e426e84909bd622f281" 600
log "pages: job 00000001 page 3 1985x2526 MD5 5c84df195515fb80d961d78c9fa8908d" 600
log "pages: job 00000001 rendered, 3 pages, PDF 32366 bytes, [0-9]+ us, longest pass [0-9]+ us, 0 dots lost" 600
cardsame PRINTER/00000001.pdf tools/dev/builds/disks/escp-expected.pdf
cardnone PRINTER/*.PRN
cardnone PRINTER/*.PDT
